{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X2jnNsZ1nsP3P7igfEh5YD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tpackage com.unityinflow.sample.shipment\n2\t\n3\t/**\n4\t * A shipment raised against an order.\n5\t *\n6\t * This is the baseline (pre-benchmark) shape. BE-003 asks an agent to add a confirm\n7\t * transition; the baseline deliberately has no way to move a shipment out of [CREATED].\n8\t */\n9\tdata class Shipment(\n10\t    val shipmentId: String,\n11\t    val orderId: String,\n12\t    val carrier: String,\n13\t    val status: ShipmentStatus,\n14\t)\n15\t\n16\t/**\n17\t * The lifecycle of a shipment.\n18\t *\n19\t * [CANCELLED] is terminal. It is reachable in the fixture only by writing it directly to\n20\t * the repository — there is no cancel endpoint — which is enough for a test to set up the\n21\t * state without giving the benchmark a second unrelated feature to implement.\n22\t */\n23\tenum class ShipmentStatus {\n24\t    CREATED,\n25\t    CONFIRMED,\n26\t    CANCELLED,\n27\t}\n28\t\n29\tdata class CreateShipmentRequest(\n30\t    val shipmentId: String,\n31\t    val orderId: String,\n32\t    val carrier: String,\n33\t)\n34\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DpQjd3E2DPeegshTK1uDgr","session_id":"fcff379c-4202-4774-b9ca-fe61e7dad979","uuid":"da851d1c-9817-4c4c-98a5-3d8f28c8009e","timestamp":"2026-09-07T12:40:09.620Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore shipment feature structure and find key files"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cep6S76xsMsRUjnLmNYWJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've launched an exploration agent to map out the shipment feature structure. It's searching for key files like the shipment controller, entity, service, repository, and test files.\n\nOnce it completes, I'll:\n1. Review the current shipment architecture\n2. Understand the existing status handling\n3. Add the `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint\n4. Implement the status transition logic (CREATED → CONFIRMED, with idempotency)\n5. Add proper error handling (409 for CANCELLED, 404 for not found)\n6. Run tests to verify everything works\n\nStanding by for the exploration results..."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22,"cache_read_input_tokens":27908,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcff379c-4202-4774-b9ca-fe61e7dad979","uuid":"117f8721-4d84-4be0-ab17-b7c011856ab6","timestamp":"2026-09-07T12:40:10.592Z","request_id":"req_011Cep6S6Np1JtS7kQFLYsRi"}
